	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "38dabd65-03d6-4724-8850-32b3bf257469",
		"name": "CMS Blue Button API Local (v3)",
		"description": "To use this Postman collection to query the Blue Button Local, follow the instructions below.\n\nYou will NOT need to create an application since this is automatically done after spinning up the container locally on localhost:8000.\n    \n1. Select the top-level folder in this Postman collection (**CMS Blue Button API Local (v3)**)\n    \n2. Select the **Variables** tab.\n    \n3. Copy the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** from `TestApp` into `Values` fields of the corresponding Postman variables (`clientId` and `clientSecret`).\n    \n4. Select the `Authorization` tab\n    \n5. Click **Get New Access Token**.\n    \n6. Choose the Login `Medicare` option\n    \n7. A Medicare login screen will open. Enter the username and password for a Local synthetic user account (e.g., user = \"BBUser00000\" and password = \"PW00000!\"), and click **Log in**.\n    \n8. Click **Connect**.\n    \n9. Click **Use Token** and make any desired Blue Button API calls under the **Patient**, **Explanation Of Benefit**, **Coverage**, and **Audit Event** folders.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "19801584"
	},
